nal of Geophysical Research Atmospheres,\n119\n(13), 7773–7798.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/2013JD021084\nArticle\nGoogle Scholar\nPichon, A. L., Ceranna, L., Pilger, C., Mialle, P., Brown, D., Herry, P., & Brachet, N. (2013). The 2013 Russian fireball largest ever detected by CTBTO infrasound sensors.\nGeophysical Research Letters,\n40\n(14), 3732–3737.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/grl.50619\nArticle\nGoogle Scholar\nPrior, M., Meless, O., Bittner, P., & Sugioka, H. (2011). Long-range detection and location of shallow underwater explosions using deep-sound-channel hydrophones.\nIEEE Journal of Oceanic Engineering,\n36\n, 703–715.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1109/JOE.2011.2154390\nArticle\nGoogle Scholar\nPsyllides G (2011) Evangelos Florakis blast kills 12, Cyprus Mail Co. Ltd., 11 July 2011\nReagan M (2006) Petrology, geochemistry, and tectonic implications of newly collected samples from Babeldaob Island, Republic of Palau, American Geophysical Union, Fall Meeting 2006, abstract id. V41B-1708\nStevens, J. L., Hanson, J., Nielsen, P., Zampolli, M., Le Bras, R., Haralabus, G., & Day, S. M. (2021). Calculation of hydroacoustic propagation and conversion to seismic phases at T-stations.\nPure and Applied Geophysics,\n178\n, 2579–2609.\nArticle\nGoogle Scholar\nSykes, L. R., & Ewig, M. (1965). The seismicity of the Caribbean Region.\nJournal Geophysics Research\n.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1029/JZ070i020p05065\nArticle\nGoogle Scholar\nTalandier, J., & Okal, E. A. (1998). On the Mechanism of Conversion of Seismic Waves to and from T Waves in the Vicinity of Island Shores.\nBulletin of the Seismological Society of America,\n88\n(2), 621–632.\nArticle\nGoogle Scholar\nTribou R (2021) Another massive explosion off coast of Florida hits 3.9 on Richter scale,\nhttps://www.stripes.com/theaters/us/2021-07-16/ocean-explosion-navy-2170235.html\nWalker, K. T., Pichon, A. L., Kim, T. S., Che, Y., & Garcés, M. (2013). An analysis of ground shaking and transmission loss from infrasound generated by the 2011 Tohoku earthquake.\nJournal Geophysics Research Atmosphere,\n118\n(23), 12831–12851.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/2013JD020187\nArticle\nGoogle Scholar\nDownload references\nAcknowledgements\nThe authors express their sincere appreciation to the reviewers for their insightful reviews. We are also grateful to all CTBTO colleagues who contributed to the IMS monitoring system, IDC data processing and data analysis. The views expressed on this paper are those of the authors and do not necessarily reflect the views of the organizations that the authors represent.\nFunding\nNo funding was provided for the completion of this study.\nAuthor information\nAuthors and Affiliations\nInternational Data Centre, MDA, CTBTO Preparatory Commission, 1400, Vienna, Austria\nPaulina Bittner, Sherif M. Ali, Ali Kasmi, Marcela Villarroel, Ehsan Qorbani & Ivana Jukic\nNational Research Institute of Astronomy and Geophysics (NRIAG), Helwan, Cairo, 11421, Egypt\nSherif M. Ali\nAuthors\nPaulina Bittner\nView author publications\nSearch author on:\nPubMed\nGoogle Scholar\nSherif M. Ali\nView author publications\nSearch author on:\nPubMed\nGoogle Scholar\nAli Kasmi\nView author publications\nSearch author on:\nPubMed\nGoogle Scholar\nMarcela Villarroel\nView author publications\nSearch author on:\nPubMed\nGoogle Scholar\nEhsan Qorbani\nView author publications\nSearch author on:\nPubMed\nGoogle Scholar\nIvana Jukic\nView author publications\nSearch author on:\nPubMed\nGoogle Scholar\nConsortia\nMonitoring and Data Analysis Team\nContributions\nPaulina Bittner and Sherif M. Ali wrote the main manuscript text, Ali Kasmi prepared Fig. 1, All authors reviewed the manuscript.\nCorresponding author\nCorrespondence to\nPaulina Bittner\n.\nEthics declarations\nConflict of interest\nThe authors declare no competing interests.\nAdditional information\nPublisher's Note\nSpringer Nature remains neutral with regard to jurisdictional claims in published maps and institutional affiliations.\nRights and per